{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgzXQCWW2vAdFhkSR6MKC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That makes sense, because nothing has been fixed yet. Last time I only looked for the cause and changed no code, so the app still behaves the way it did.\n\nI just checked the two places that write the end-of-meeting recap, and neither has changed:\n- **`electron/MeetingPersistence.ts`** (the default instructions to the AI) hasn't been touched since May. It still has no rule about tasks without a due date.\n- **`electron/llm/prompts.ts`** was modified today at 16:52, but not by me. The Groq instructions inside it (lines 370–393) are the same as before. They still don't say to keep undated tasks, and their only example task, \"Bob: Draft invite copy by Wednesday\", has a deadline. If you or someone else edited this file today, the change was in a different prompt from the one used when a meeting ends.\n\nI still can't see the bug happen myself, because there are no Groq or Gemini API keys here to run a real recap.\n\nTo fix it, I'd add the same rule the other prompts in `prompts.ts` already use to both recap prompts: \"Keep every action item that has an owner, even if it has no due date; write 'no date given'.\" I'd also change the Groq example to include one task with no date. That's a small change to the prompt text only.\n\nDo you want me to make that change now? You could then check it on your next meeting. If you'd rather I see the failure first, send me a short transcript where it happens and tell me which AI provider you use."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":935,"cache_read_input_tokens":63913,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":935},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics